WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:11.030 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the weekend is opening up about his 2018  ep  my dear melancholy which fans think  references his past  relationships with bella hadid and  selena gomez  although he didn't go into specific  details about the meaning behind the  project  he did tell esquire magazine why it was  so important for him to write and  release the record the reason why it was  so  short is like i think i just had nothing  else to say on this  it was just like this cathartic piece of  art and yeah it was sure  because that's all i had to say on this  situation  despite not speaking directly about the  lyrics on my dear melancholy  the weeknd did address some past lyrics  which have been perceived as  misogynistic  so during his candid interview one  specific line from his hit  2015 song the hills was mentioned and  when asked whether the words defined him  as a person  he said that it's definitely a character  it's like you want people to feel a  certain way  you want them to feel angry you want  them to feel sad you want them to  feel it's never like my intent to offend  anybody i'm a writer  sometimes i write a song and it's not in  my head i'm writing it for someone else  but then  i end up singing it the grammy award  winner also revealed that he plans to  write a full  album for female artists telling esquire  i want to write a whole album for female  artists  i have a whole vision of the weekend but  i guess it's like  it's the same reason why i want to write  for someone else  you

